---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
const updated = "6 September 2026";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Croodit"
  description="What Croodit collects, why, and what it never touches. Croodit sends invoices through the WhatsApp already on your phone and cannot read your chats."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated {updated}. This policy covers the Croodit mobile app and {SITE.url}.</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Croodit cannot read your WhatsApp chats. It opens WhatsApp with a message prepared; you press send.</li>
      <li>We never message your clients on your behalf. Reminders are notifications to you.</li>
      <li>We do not sell your data or your client list, to anyone, ever.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Your account:</b> phone number (verified by SMS code), business name, your name, UPI ID, optional logo, city and GSTIN if you enable GST.</li>
      <li><b>Your business records:</b> clients you add, services and prices, invoices, payments you record, attendance and expenses.</li>
      <li><b>Contacts:</b> only if you tap "From contacts". Croodit reads the contact you pick to fill in a name and number. It does not upload your address book.</li>
      <li><b>Pay-page analytics:</b> when a client opens a pay link we log that it was opened, so your invoice timeline can show it.</li>
      <li><b>App diagnostics:</b> crash and error reports, so we can fix things.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What we never collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your WhatsApp messages, contacts inside WhatsApp, or read/delivery receipts. No integration exists that would let us.</li>
      <li>Your UPI PIN, bank credentials or card details. Payments happen inside your client's own UPI app.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>
      To run the product you asked for: generate invoices and PDFs, host your pay links, schedule the reminders
      you switched on, and produce your earnings and GST summaries. We also use aggregate, non-identifying usage
      counts to decide what to build next.
    </p>

    <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
    <p>
      Only the service providers Croodit runs on — hosting, database, crash reporting, SMS delivery for your
      login code and, if you subscribe, the app store handling your payment. They process data on our
      instructions and nothing more. We disclose data to authorities only where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Where your client's payment goes</h2>
    <p>
      Straight to you. A Croodit pay link opens a standard UPI request addressed to your UPI ID. Croodit is not
      a payment gateway, never holds your money, and takes no cut of it.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      For as long as your account is open — invoices are business records you may need years later. Delete your
      account from Settings and we remove your data within 30 days, except records we must retain by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can export everything (Excel, PDF or Tally format) from Settings at any time, edit or delete any client
      or invoice, revoke contacts and notification permissions in your phone settings, and close your account.
      To ask what we hold on you, or to have it deleted, write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Croodit is a business tool and is not intended for anyone under 18.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially we will say so in the app before the change applies. Questions:
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
